# Topic 4 · Gender and Development

::: glance | Topic 4 at a glance
**Head V** of the syllabus — the **heaviest topic** in the paper: ==17.5 visits== (sixteen full questions and three short notes, 2016–2026), asked **every year**, plus 17 of the 140 MCQs. Four families: **WID/WAD/GAD** (2016, 2017 note, 2018 note on needs, 2021, 2025); **colonial and capitalist perspectives** (2020, 2022, 2023, 2024); **globalisation** (2017, 2018, 2019, 2025); **development theories** (2019, 2019 note, 2021, 2024, 2025). The command word is almost always "**critically**". The newest questions join theory to the present: development as coloniality (2024), gendered globalisation (2025), climate and floods (2026). Never yet asked in full: world-system theory alone, gender mainstreaming, the SDGs, the care economy.
:::

